    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d400">

                <pb facs="0469" n="409" xml:id="pg409"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Eustis to Mr. Gresham</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-04-08"><hi rendition="#italic">April 8,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Minister for foreign affairs says, in reply to our protest, that Canada subjects
                    American cattle to a quarantine of ninety days; that similar measures were taken
                    by several of the United States; that South Dakota prohibits their introduction;
                    that Illinois, in consequence of pleuro-pneumonia, subjects the same to a long
                    quarantine. Are these statements correct? Reply and translation mailed to you
                    April 5. Telegraph reply.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Eustis</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
